---
description: Ecommerce business rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Always preserve ecommerce business logic.

## Products

- Variants are purchasable entities.
- Product may have multiple variants.
- Stock may be `null`.
- Preorder may exist.
- Do not treat product itself as purchasable if existing code uses variants as purchasable entities.
- Preserve existing variant/product relationships.

## Orders

- Totals come from backend.
- Discounts may exist.
- Gift certificates may exist.
- Delivery fee is separate unless backend combines it.
- Do not recalculate final order totals on frontend unless existing code already does it.
- Backend is the source of truth for totals, discounts, delivery fees, and final prices.

## Cart / Checkout

- Preserve existing checkout flow.
- Preserve existing cart item identity logic.
- Preserve variant-based cart logic.
- Do not change price calculation logic unless explicitly requested.
- Do not change API contracts unless explicitly requested.

## Money

- Money values may come as strings.
- Do not use float math for prices.
- Preserve precision.
- Avoid converting price strings to floats for calculations.